{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The test `TestSenseLoopTemplateHasBackflowAndSystemDescriptor` checks the raw TEMPLATE content (not the rendered output) for `{{max_backflows}}`. So that test checks the template still contains the variable placeholder. That's fine — it tests the template, not the rendered output.\n\nThe issue is the dry-run rendered output. The `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt` (dry-run path) doesn't set `max_backflows`, so the rendered output has unresolved `{{max_backflows}}`.\n\nThe fix: add `builder.SetVariable(\"max_backflows\", \"3\")` to `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt`. Also `min_assumptions` is used in think.md but that's a separate subagent prompt (not rendered in the main sense_loop dry-run). Actually the dry-run only renders sense_loop, which uses `max_backflows`, `max_retries` (already set to \"5\"), and the agent paths, topic, rfc_dir, draft_dir, loop_dir.\n\nSo the minimal fix for the dry-run is to add `builder.SetVariable(\"max_backflows\", \"3\")` in `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt`.\n\nLet me verify this is the right fix by checking the config default. The config default is `SenseMaxBackflows: 3`. The `GenerateHumanLoopPromptFile` hardcodes \"3\" for max_backflows too. So adding \"3\" to the dry-run is consistent.\n\nActually wait — let me look more carefully. The `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt` also doesn't set `min_assumptions`. But `min_assumptions` is only in think.md, which is not part of the main sense_loop dry-run output. So it's fine.\n\nSo the fix is:\n1. In `internal/prompt/human_loop_prompt.go`, `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt`, add `builder.SetVariable(\"max_backflows\", \"3\")`.\n\nLet me verify there are no other unresolved vars by checking what `GenerateHumanLoopPrompt` sets vs what sense_loop.md uses.\n\nsense_loop.md vars: topic, rfc_dir, draft_dir, loop_dir, think_agent_path, research_agent_path, exporter_agent_path, max_retries, max_backflows.\n\n`GenerateHumanLoopPrompt` sets: top