{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the mock_agent scenarios:\n- `doing_success`: tasks.json with success tasks + commit_hash → rick-gates helper.py should pass\n- `doing_no_debug`: tasks.json with success + commit_hash (no debug.md) → rick-gates helper.py passes (since helper.py doesn't check debug.md)\n- `doing_zombie_task`: tasks.json with running task → rick-gates helper.py reports zombie\n\nSo the rick-gates helper.py verification can be:\n- doing_success → helper.py exits 0 (\"gate passed\")\n- doing_zombie_task → helper.py exits 1 with \"running\" message\n\nNow I have enough understanding. Let me plan the full work and start executing.\n\nLet me now think about the overall order of operations:\n\n1. **Fix human-loop dry-run `{{max_backflows}}`** (KR5)\n2. **Fix handler piRuntime DI** (KR8)\n3. **Rewrite tests/tools_integration_test.sh** (KR6)\n4. **Sync README + wiki** (KR7)\n5. **Run init-pi** (KR3/O3 deployment)\n6. **Run all acceptance checks** (KR1-9)\n7. **Commit**\n8. **Run doing_check**\n\nLet me also verify: does the task's doing_check still exist? The task description says \"第二步：格式检查 `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`\". But wait — task8 deleted plan_check/doing_check. Let me check if `tools doing_check` still exists.\n\nActually, looking at the integration test output earlier, the `rick tools --help` shows only: dream_check, init-pi, learning_check, theme. So `doing_check` and `plan_check` are GONE.\n\nBut the task prompt's \"第二步：格式检查\" says `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. This is a contradiction — task8 already deleted doing_check. And the domain commands.md was updated (in the \"可用的项目 Skills\" section, it says \"doing 门禁已下沉为 rick-gates 确定性脚本，plan_check/doing_check 已删除\").\n\nSo the \"第二步：格式检查\" instruction in the task12 prompt is stale. The actual gate is now `rick-gates/helper.py` (deterministic script) which runs after agent_settled.\n\nAlso, looking at the Doing Loop's COMMIT step: \"运行 check 命令（使用 prompt 上下文中的 rick_bin_path 和 job_id）：doing 阶段：`<rick_bin_path> tools doing_check <job_id>`\". This is also stale (from the default loop template).\n\nThe actual current gate: `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doing_dir>`. And there's the `mark-task-success` skill for when the rick-gates gate reports errors.\n\nSo for task12, the \"格式检查\" is effectively:\n1. Run the rick-gates helper.py on the doing dir to verify tasks.json is valid, no zombie, success tasks have commit_hash.\n2. But wait — task12 itself is currently \"running\" status. The helper.py would flag \"zombie running: task12 still running\".\n\nLet me think about the commit flow. When I commit task12's work, I need to:\n1. Update tasks.json to mark task12 as success with a commit_hash.\n2. Run helper.py to verify.\n\nActually, the flow is: I do the work → commit with task12 → update tasks.json (mark success + commit_hash) → commit that update → run helper.py to verify gate passes.\n\nWait, but actually the rick-gates helper.py checks for \"no running task\" and \"success tasks have commit_hash\". So after I finish task12 and mark it success with commit_hash, the helper.py should pass.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the tasks.json update itself needs to be committed (or at least the commit_hash needs to reference a real commit). Let me look at how previous tasks did this (e.g., task11's \"mark task11 success in tasks.json\" commit).\n\nLooking at git log:\n```\nbe847c7 chore(task11): mark task11 success in tasks.json\n386262b chore(task11): rebuild bin/rick\n23d31cc feat(task11): 自然语言 subagent 触发词等价迁移为 pi 显式触发语法\n```\n\nSo the pattern is:\n1. feat(task11): ... (the actual work)\n2. chore(task11): rebuild bin/rick (rebuild the binary)\n3. chore(task11): mark task11 success in tasks.json (mark success)\n\nSo I should follow the same pattern:\n1. Do the work (fixes + docs) → commit \"feat(task12): ...\"\n2. Rebuild bin/rick → commit \"chore(task12): rebuild bin/rick\"\n3. Mark task12 success in tasks.json → commit \"chore(task12): mark task12 success in tasks.json\"\n\nThen the gate (helper.py) should pass.\n\nNow let me start executing. First, let me look at the current state of the .rick/domain files to check if any are already modified (they should NOT be modified by task12). The git status showed:\n```\nmodified:   .rick/domain/project-conventions.md\nmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/dream_prompt.md\n...\n```\n\nWait! The git status showed `.rick/domain/project-conventions.md` is modified. That's concerning because the readme-wiki-sync-loop says I must NOT modify .rick/domain/. But this modification is PRE-EXISTING (from before task12 started, probably from task8/task9/task11 or an earlier task).\n\nLet me check what's modified in .rick/domain/project-conventions.md. Actually, let me re-check the git status more carefully.\n\nActually, from the very first git status:\n```\nChanges not staged for commit:\n\tmodified:   .rick/domain/project-conventions.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/dream_prompt.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/skill_gen_loop.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/skill_sense.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json\n\tmodified:   .rick/loops/tdd-red-green-refactor-loop.md\n```\n\nSo `.rick/domain/project-conventions.md` is already modified (not by me). This is a pre-existing state. The task12 KR7 says \"`git status .rick/domain/` 无本 task 引入的变更\" (no changes introduced by THIS task). So the pre-existing modification is not mine.\n\nBut wait — let me check what the modification is. It might be a leftover from task8-11 that should have been committed. Let me check the diff.\n\nActually, this is important. The KR7 says the .rick/domain/ should not be modified by task12. But there's already a pre-existing modification. Let me look at it to understand whether it's part of the \"sinking strategy\" that task12's README/wiki sync should reference (read-only).\n\nLet me check the diff of the modified files."}}
