 Mark task12 success in tasks.json → commit \"chore(task12): mark task12 success in tasks.json\"\n\nThen the gate (helper.py) should pass.\n\nNow let me start executing. First, let me look at the current state of the .rick/domain files to check if any are already modified (they should NOT be modified by task12). The git status showed:\n```\nmodified:   .rick/domain/project-conventions.md\nmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/dream_prompt.md\n...\n```\n\nWait! The git status showed `.rick/domain/project-conventions.md` is modified. That's concerning because the readme-wiki-sync-loop says I must NOT modify .rick/domain/. But this modification is PRE-EXISTING (from before task12 started, probably from task8/task9/task11 or an earlier task).\n\nLet me check what's modified in .rick/domain/project-conventions.md. Actually, let me re-check the git status more carefully.\n\nActually, from the very first git status:\n```\nChanges not staged for commit:\n\tmodified:   .rick/domain/project-conventions.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/dream_prompt.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/skill_gen_loop.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/dream/prompts/skill_sense.md\n\tmodified:   .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json\n\tmodified:   .rick/loops/tdd-red-green-refactor-loop.md\n```\n\nSo `.rick/domain/project-conventions.md` is already modified (not by me). This is a pre-existing state. The task12 KR7 says \"`git status .rick/domain/` 无本 task 引入的变更\" (no changes introduced by THIS task). So the pre-existing modification is not mine.\n\nBut wait — let me check what the modification is. It might be a leftover from task8-11 that should have been committed. Let me check the diff.\n\nActually, this is important. The KR7 says the .rick/domain/ should not be modified by task12. But there's already a pre-existing modification. Let me look at it to understand whether it's part of the \"sinking strategy\" that task12's README/wiki sync should reference (read-only).\n\nLet me check the diff of the modified 