{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The wiki is very outdated and extensive (10k+ lines). This is a big task to fully sync. Let me think about the most efficient, correct approach.\n\nThe task says: \"README.md + wiki/ 同步三层金字塔 + spec 信息内核 + env 四职责 + 下沉策略（只读引用 .rick/domain/，不写）\".\n\nThe readme-wiki-sync-loop's CLEANUP step says: \"检查 README.md 和 wiki/ 中是否引用已删除的旧架构概念... 检查 wiki/ 下是否有重复或过时文件，直接删除(不留 TODO)\".\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Remove old module files (modules/executor.md, modules/git.md, modules/parser.md) — these reference deleted packages.\n2. Update wiki/README.md to reflect the new structure.\n3. Update wiki/architecture.md to reflect three-layer pyramid + spec info kernel + env four responsibilities + sinking strategy.\n4. Update other wiki files that reference old concepts (dag-execution, runtime-flow, prompt-system, testing).\n5. Update README.md.\n\nThis is a large amount of documentation work. Given the scope, I'll focus on:\n1. The most important sync: README.md (project entry) and wiki/architecture.md + wiki/README.md.\n2. Remove clearly obsolete module files (executor/git/parser).\n3. Update the modules index.\n4. Add a new \"modules\" section reflecting the new architecture (cmd/handler/env/builder/runtime/prompt/workspace/config).\n5. Update other wiki files' outdated references (dag-execution → sinking strategy, etc.).\n\nActually, let me be strategic. The key requirement (KR7) is:\n\"README.md + wiki/ 同步三层金字塔 + spec 信息内核 + env 四职责 + 下沉策略（只读引用 .rick/domain/，不写）；git status .rick/domain/ 无本 task 引入的变更\"\n\nSo the deliverables are:\n1. README.md synced with: 三层金字塔 (three-layer pyramid), spec 信息内核 (spec info kernel), env 四职责 (env four responsibilities), 下沉策略 (sinking strategy).\n2. wiki/ synced with the same.\n3. .rick/domain/ unchanged.\n\nThe \"只读引用 .rick/domain/，不写\" means the docs should reference .rick/domain/ as a read-only fact source (not write to it).\n\nLet me focus on a clean, correct rewrite of:\n1. README.md — update the architecture section (三层金字塔), add spec 信息内核 section, env 四职责, 下沉策略. Remove old references (executor, parser, actpath, git, agent, DAG).\n2. wiki/README.md — update index/navigation.\n3. wiki/architecture.md — rewrite with three-layer pyramid.\n4. Delete wiki/modules/executor.md, wiki/modules/git.md, wiki/modules/parser.md.\n5. Add wiki/modules/{handler,env,builder,runtime}.md (new modules).\n6. Update wiki/modules/cmd.md, config.md, workspace.md, prompt.md, human-loop.md to reflect new reality.\n7. Update wiki/dag-execution.md → replace with sinking strategy (or rewrite as a new doc about pi workflowScript orchestration).\n8. Update wiki/runtime-flow.md, prompt-system.md, testing.md as needed.\n\nThis is a LOT. Let me be efficient and prioritize the files that clearly violate the \"no outdated concepts\" rule.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the scope and what's realistic. The readme-wiki-sync-loop requires:\n- 无过时或无用记录残留(旧架构概念、废弃 flag、已删除目录、过时版本号)\n- README.md 与 wiki/ 之间无内容矛盾\n\nThe wiki files reference: executor, parser, git, DAG, .rick/wiki/, SPEC.md, OKR.md, v1.0.0-dev, Claude Code CLI, etc. These are all outdated.\n\nGiven the volume, I'll do a focused rewrite of the key files and delete the clearly-obsolete ones. Let me check the total size and plan.\n\nLet me first look at what modules files exist and their sizes, and decide the plan.\n\nActually, the most efficient approach given the constraints:\n\n1. **Rewrite README.md** — comprehensive, accurate, reflecting the new architecture. This is the most important deliverable.\n2. **Rewrite wiki/README.md** — index with correct structure.\n3. **Rewrite wiki/architecture.md** — three-layer pyramid.\n4. **Delete** wiki/modules/executor.md, wiki/modules/git.md, wiki/modules/parser.md (obsolete modules).\n5. **Rewrite wiki/modules/cmd.md, config.md, workspace.md, prompt.md, human-loop.md** — or at least ensure they don't reference deleted concepts.\n6. **Replace wiki/dag-execution.md** — since DAG execution is now sunk to pi workflowScript. Rename/rewrite to reflect sinking strategy. Actually, the file name \"dag-execution.md\" is itself outdated (DAG was deleted). I should delete it or rewrite it as \"orchestration.md\".\n\nLet me check the modules/*.md files to see their content and decide.\n\nActually, this is getting very large. Let me be pragmatic and focus on producing correct, consistent docs. I'll:\n\n1. Rewrite README.md (main deliverable).\n2. Rewrite wiki/README.md.\n3. Rewrite wiki/architecture.md.\n4. Rewrite the modules/*.md (delete obsolete, rewrite others).\n5. Rewrite/delete dag-execution.md.\n6. Lightly update runtime-flow.md, prompt-system.md, testing.md, installation.md (or rewrite if heavily outdated).\n\nLet me read the modules/*.md files first to understand what to keep/delete."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_AHVETpL6QvglWmh4Ng0d3214","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && wc -l wiki/*.md wiki/modules/*.md && echo \"=== grep outdated concepts across wiki ===\" && grep -rln 'executor\\|parser\\|internal/git\\|\\.rick/wiki\\|SPEC\\.md\\|OKR\\.md\\|v1\\.0\\.0-dev\\|DAG\\|Claude Code\\|claudecode\\|callcli\\|actpath\\|internal/agent' wiki/ | sort"}}}}
