{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The wiki validation now passes correctly with 24 code examples and 0 errors.\n\nNow let me proceed to the remaining tasks:\n\n1. Run `rick tools init-pi` to deploy agents/extensions (KR3/O3).\n2. Run all acceptance checks (KR1-KR9).\n3. Verify the natural language trigger decline (already checked by task12.py, but let me verify).\n4. Commit + gate.\n\nFirst, let me run `rick tools init-pi` to deploy the pi agents and extensions. But wait — this requires node/npm and might install things. The runtime is already installed (~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime exists). Let me run it.\n\nActually, before that, let me check if there's a concern: running init-pi might try to install packages if missing, which needs network. But pi-subagents and pi-web-access are already installed (from earlier ls of node_modules). Let me just run it and see.\n\nActually, the O3 check (KR3) says: \"显式 export RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR=<temp>（或改用 ~/.rick/pi/agent 默认路径）后，$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/agents/{think,research,exporter}.md 3 文件存在 + $RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/extensions/rick-gates/ 已部署\".\n\nThe task12.py test already verifies this via the deploy (it passed). But the ACTUAL runtime deployment to ~/.rick/pi/agent hasn't happened yet (the agents/ and extensions/ dirs don't exist there). The KR says to run init-pi (or use RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR temp).\n\nLet me run `rick tools init-pi` to deploy to the real ~/.rick/pi/agent. This is part of KR9 (真实运行验收) too.\n\nLet me run init-pi now."}}
