\n=== rick agents source ===\ninternal/builder/orchestration.go:199:\tsb.WriteString(\"你是本次 job 的 parent 编排者（单写者）。必须调用 `subagent` 工具，把下面的 `workflowScript` 作为其 `workflowScript` 参数触发编排执行（一次触发，内部按依赖拓扑顺序执行，`await` 强制顺序，被依赖 task 先执行；每个 task 完成后由 worker 立即 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent 写入 tasks.json）。\\n\\n\")\ninternal/builder/orchestration.go:204:\t\tsb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf(\"const %s = await runs.run('%s', {agent:'worker', task:'按 %s 执行 %s，完成后 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent 写入 tasks.json'});\\n\",\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917310695}}
{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pi API is functional — deepseek responds correctly, and the event stream ends with `agent_settled`. The event stream is exactly as the runtime parser expects (session header, message_start/end, agent_settled, camelCase fields).\n\nSo I CAN do a real run. Now let me create a minimal test job and run `rick doing` on it to verify the full workflow.\n\nLet me create a minimal test job. I need:\n1. `.rick/jobs/job_accept/plan/task1.md` — a trivial task.\n2. Run `rick doing job_accept` from the project root (so it uses the project's .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py, loops, skills, domain).\n\nWait, but running from the project root means the job would be `.rick/jobs/job_accept` in the project. That's fine — I can clean it up after (or leave it as a test job).\n\nActually, I should be careful: running `rick doing job_accept` from the project root would:\n1. Use project's .rick (loops/skills/domain/rick-gates all present).\n2. Create `.rick/jobs/job_accept/doing/`.\n3. Generate doing prompt with workflowScript for task1.\n4. Run pi (real deepseek call).\n5. The pi parent would run the workflowScript via subagent, dispatching a worker to execute task1.\n6. The worker would do the task (trivial), commit, write commit_hash.\n7. After settle, gate runs.\n\nThis is a real end-to-end test. The task should be TRIVIAL so the worker can complete it quickly (e.g., \"create a file named acceptance.txt with content OK\").\n\nLet me create the test job. The task.md format (from the doing_loop / EnsureTasksJSON scanPlanOrchTasks):\n```\n# 依赖关系\n无\n# 任务名称\nAcceptance test\n# 任务目标\nCreate a file\n# 关键结果\n1. acceptance.txt created\n# 测试方法\ntest -f acceptance.txt\n```\n\nActually, let me check the exact format expected. From scanPlanOrchTasks, it extracts \"# 依赖关系\" section. And the worker reads the task file. The task file format is:\n- # 依赖关系\n- # 任务名称\n- # 任务目标\n- # 关键结果\n- # 测试方法\n\nLet me create this test job.\n\nActually, wait — let me reconsider the risk. A real `rick doing` run:\n1. The pi parent will be instructed to call the `subagent` tool with workflowScript.\n2. This requires the pi-subagents extension to be loaded (it is, per init-pi).\n3. The worker agent ('worker') must be configured. Is there a 'worker' agent? The workflowScript uses `agent:'worker'`. Let me check if the 'worker' agent exists in the pi configuration.\n\nLooking at the doing prompt's workflowScript: `runs.run('task1', {agent:'worker', task:'...'})`. The 'worker' agent must be a configured agent in pi. Let me check what agents are configured.\n\nActually, from the pi-subagents skill, there's a default 'worker' agent? Or maybe rick deploys a 'worker' agent via env. Let me check the env agents — I saw think/research/exporter agents deployed. But 'worker'?\n\nHmm, wait. Let me check the pi-subagents extension to understand what agents are available by default.\n\nActually, let me check the ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/ — it has think.md, research.md, exporter.md (deployed by rick). No 'worker'.\n\nBut the workflowScript references `agent:'worker'`. So there must be a 'worker' agent somewhere. Let me check the pi-subagents package or rick's agent deployment.\n\nLet me look for 'worker' agent definition.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_YBixUVRG7dG7TEc0LmWQ1456","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== agents deployed ===\" && ls ~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== search 'worker' in pi-subagents ===\" && grep -rn 'worker' ~/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/ 2>/dev/null | grep -i 'agent\\|worker' | head -20; echo \"=== rick agents source ===\" && grep -rn 'worker' internal/env/*.go internal/builder/*.go | head"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1005,"output":1001,"cacheRead":197760,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":833,"totalTokens":199766,"cost":{"input":0.00043717500000000004,"output":0.00087087,"cacheRead":0.00071688,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0020249250000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786917297684,"responseId":"d41b745e-3f17-4d91-8341-c42247e54907","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_YBixUVRG7dG7TEc0LmWQ1456","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== agents deployed ===\nexporter.md\nresearch.md\nthink.md\n=== search 'worker' in pi-subagents ===\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:96:- Drop late workflow child responses after worker settlement. Thanks to @xz-dev (Xiangzhe) for #922.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:191:- Added trusted inline `workflowScript` orchestration with stable-key child launches through the ordinary executor, timed worker isolation, captured console and emitted milestones, artifact references, status lookup, and a concise call trace.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:241:- Count clear `git add`, `git commit`, and `git push` bash calls as implementation mutation attempts so workers that finalize pre-applied changes do not fail the completion guard.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:274:- Added agent frontmatter aliases and built-in worker aliases for `developer`, `coder`, `implementer`, and `develop`, while keeping canonical names in execution state. Thanks to @selimerunkut for #695.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:326:- Refreshed the bundled `pi-subagents` skill for 0.35–0.37 control and config surface: `/subagents`, `/subagents-stop`, `/subagents-watchdog`, `stop`/`append-step`, parallel `count`, watchdog overview, frontmatter `async`/`timeoutMs`/`turnBudget` defaults, `artifactDir`/`asyncWidget`, fresh/fork badges, and builtin worker/delegate ambient-tool boundaries.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:347:- Documented that builtin worker and delegate agents use strict tool allowlists and do not inherit ambient parent extension tools; custom agents must explicitly name extension tools and load their providers. Thanks to buihongduc132 for #586.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:400:- Registered the native child `intercom` fallback before strict tool-allowlist diagnostics run and stopped treating Pi core tools as missing extension tools, preventing read-only scouts and workers from failing before execution when strict child tool allowlists are active.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:404:- Recognize Cursor edit/write thinking traces and replay tool calls as mutation evidence, so Cursor-provider workers that actually edit files no longer false-fail with `completed-without-making-edits`. Thanks to Mikhail Wijanarko (@mwijanarko1) for #539.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:428:- Deferred hard turn-budget termination when an assistant starts tool work at the limit, exposing `termination-deferred` until the next safe assistant boundary while elapsed timeout and explicit stop retain precedence. Guidance now conservatively keeps hard turn and tool-call caps off mutation-capable workers. Thanks to JT (@juicetin) for #482 and #483.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:607:- Added regression coverage for long worker/reviewer chains and parallel -> funnel -> fanout chain flows across foreground and async execution.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/CHANGELOG.md:610:- Interrupt live async children before delivering `resume` follow-up messages so intercom nudges reach workers that are stuck mid-turn more reliably.\n/home/hadoop-recsys/.rick/pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-subagents/