{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"validateJobID allows alphanumeric + underscore + hyphen, so \"job_accept\" is valid.\n\nLet me create the test job and run the real doing. I'll create a minimal task.\n\nLet me create:\n1. `.rick/jobs/job_accept/plan/task1.md`\n2. Run `./bin/rick doing job_accept`\n\nThe task file:\n```\n# 依赖关系\n无\n\n# 任务名称\nAcceptance smoke test\n\n# 任务目标\n在 .rick/jobs/job_accept/doing/ 目录下创建 acceptance.txt 文件，内容为字符串 OK\n\n# 关键结果\n1. .rick/jobs/job_accept/doing/acceptance.txt 存在且内容为 OK\n\n# 测试方法\ntest -f .rick/jobs/job_accept/doing/acceptance.txt && grep -q OK .rick/jobs/job_accept/doing/acceptance.txt\n```\n\nLet me create this and run the doing command with a generous timeout.\n\nActually, I realize I should think about whether the worker will actually be able to commit. The worker needs to git add + commit. The repo has a lot of uncommitted changes (my task12 changes, plus pre-existing changes). If the worker does `git add .` + commit, it would commit ALL my changes! That's dangerous.\n\nWait, but the worker is instructed to \"完成后 commit 并把 commit_hash 回传给 parent\". The worker would do `git add <file>` + `git commit`. If the worker is careful, it only adds its own file. But there's a risk it does `git add -A` and commits everything.\n\nHmm, this is a real risk. The repo currently has:\n- My uncommitted task12 changes (code + docs + tests).\n- Pre-existing uncommitted changes (.rick/domain/project-conventions.md, dream prompts, etc.).\n\nIf the worker runs `git add -A && git commit`, it would commit ALL of this, mixing my task12 work with a test commit. That would be bad.\n\nTo avoid this risk, I should run the acceptance test in an ISOLATED git repo, not the project repo.\n\nLet me create a temp directory with:\n1. Its own git repo.\n2. `.rick/jobs/job_accept/plan/task1.md`.\n3. `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` (copy from project).\n4. `.rick/loops/` (optional, can be empty).\n