ADME (which I updated): the doing 产出 includes \"session_id（pi 会话 UUID）\". And the KR9 explicitly says \"doing/session_id 落盘\".\n\nThe spec §3.4: \"handler 持久化 = sessionID 写入 job 目录\".\n\nSo yes, the doing workflow should persist sessionID. Currently it doesn't. This is a genuine gap I need to fix.\n\nLet me fix handler/doing.go to persist sessionID to doing/session_id after a successful run.\n\nThe fix: in `Doing`, after `rt.Run` returns sessionID, write it to `doingDir/session_id`.\n\n```go\nsessionID, _, err := rt.Run(method, promptFile, cfg)\nif err != nil {\n    ...\n}\nif sessionID != \"\" {\n    if err := saveSessionID(doingDir, sessionID); err != nil {\n        // warn but don't fail\n        fmt.Printf(\"[WARN] failed to persist session_id: %v\\n\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `saveSessionID` function is already defined in easy.go (same package `handler`). So I can reuse it.\n\nWait, let me verify saveSessionID is in the same package. easy.go is in `internal/handler` package. doing.go is also `internal/handler`. So `saveSessionID` is accessible.\n\nLet me check the easy.go saveSessionID signature:\n```go\nfunc saveSessionID(doingDir, sessionID string) error {\n\treturn os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(doingDir, \"session_id\"), []byte(sessionID), 0644)\n}\n```\n\nYes, it's in the same package.\n\nLet me fix doing.go to persist sessionID.\n\nActually, let me re-read the handler doing.go to find the exact location.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_g2tdigQI4O8KWLSo2rO84968","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/handler/doing.go","offset":78,"limit":40}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":245,"output":964,"cacheRead":205056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":869,"totalTokens":206265,"cost":{"input":0.000106575,"output":0.0008386800000000001,"cacheRead":0.000743328,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001688583}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786