piRuntime.Run(...)` — line 77\n\nSo yes, 2 hits.\n\nTo fix this, I should change the handler to depend on the `Runtime` interface. The composition root (cmd) should instantiate `runtime.NewPiRuntime` and inject it.\n\nLet me look at how the handler and cmd are currently wired.\n\nLet me read doing.go, options.go, and cmd/doing.go, cmd/root.go.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_VxhrXKQPkX1IkO3vql6r0907","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/handler/doing.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_nQP2K1UjS9O8pSUKIEsj7895","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/handler/options.go"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_02_TQ5auKzlDTRtIpNHJJz04673","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/cmd/doing.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1894,"output":1638,"cacheRead":65664,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1477,"totalTokens":69196,"cost":{"input":0.0008238900000000001,"output":0.0014250600000000001,"cacheRead":0.000238032,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0024869820000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786916476727,"responseId":"4f24ca71-b431-43be-b71b-90a02ad27957","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_VxhrXKQPkX1IkO3vql6r0907","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package handler\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/builder\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\n)\n\n// Doing executes the complete doing workflow. Scheduling is now delegated to\n// pi's workflowScript orchestration (parent single-writer + runs.run with await),\n// and the gate is a deterministic rick-side script run after the pi session\n// settles. rick's retry loop is only a safety net: it regenerates an\n// orchestration of the remaining pending tasks on each attempt, bounded by\n// cfg.MaxRetries.\nfunc Doing(jobID string, opts Options) error {\n\tcfg, err := config.LoadConfig()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load config: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to get rick directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tjobDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID)\n\tplanDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"plan\")\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(jobDir, \"doing\")\n\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(jobDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job directory not found: %s\", jobDir)\n\t}\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(planDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"plan directory not found: %s\", planDir)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(doingDir, 0755); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create doing directory: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tif opts.Verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Job directory: %s\\n\", jobDir)\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Plan directory: %s\\n\", planDir)\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Doing directory: %s\\n\", doingDir)\n\t}\n\n\t// Initial tasks.json draft: builder scans plan/task*.md (all pending).\n\tif err := builder.EnsureTasksJSON(doingDir, planDir); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to initialize tasks.json: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tmaxRetries := cfg.MaxRetries\n\tif maxRetries <= 0 {\n\t\tmaxRetries = 3\n\t}\n\n\tpiRuntime := runtime.NewPiRuntime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...)\n\n\tfor attempt := 1; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++ {\n\t\tif opts.Verbose {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Attempt %d/%d\\n\", attempt, maxRetries)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// builder regenerates an orchestration of only the remaining pending\n\t\t// tasks (completed tasks are filtered out at generation time).\n\t\tpromptFile, method, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(doingDir, planDir, rickDir, jobID)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build doing prompt: %w\", err)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t_, _, err = piRuntime.Run(method, promptFile, cfg)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] pi run did not settle (attempt %d/%d): %v\\n\", attempt, maxRetries, err)\n\t\t\tif attempt < maxRetries {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"pi run failed after %d attempts: %w\", maxRetries, err)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Deterministic gate after the session settles (agent_settled).\n\t\tif gateErr := runDoingGate(rickDir, doingDir); gateErr != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[WARN] gate failed (attempt %d/%d): %v\\n\", attempt, maxRetries, gateErr)\n\t\t\tif attempt < maxRetries {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"doing gate failed after %d attempts: %w\", maxRetries, gateErr)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Job %s execution completed!\\n\", jobID)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job execution incomplete after %d attempts\", maxRetries)\n}\n\n// runDoingGate runs the deterministic rick-side gate script:\n// python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doingDir>. Exit non-zero = gate\n// failure (unparseable tasks.json / zombie running / success without commit_hash).\nfunc runDoingGate(rickDir, doingDir string) error {\n\thelper := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\", \"rick-gates\", \"helper.py\")\n\tcmd := exec.Command(\"python3\", helper, doingDir)\n\tout, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tmsg := strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n\t\tif msg == \"\" {\n\t\t\tmsg = err.Error()\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s\", msg)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// DoingDryRun generates and prints the doing prompt (with the pi workflowScript\n// orchestration) without executing it.\nfunc DoingDryRun(jobID string) error {\n\tif jobID == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"[DRY-RUN] No job ID provided\")\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to get rick dir: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tplanDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"plan\")\n\tif _, err := os.Stat(planDir); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\tdoingDirFallback := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\t\tif _, e := os.Stat(filepath.Join(doingDirFallback, \"requirement.md\")); e == nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] %s is an easy mode job (no plan/). Use: rick doing --easy --dry-run\\n\", jobID)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] plan directory not found: %s\\n\", planDir)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tdoingDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"jobs\", jobID, \"doing\")\n\n\tpromptFile, _, _, err := builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(doingDir, planDir, rickDir, jobID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to generate prompt: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tcontent, err := os.ReadFile(promptFile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] failed to read prompt file: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\n\tfmt.Printf(\"[DRY-RUN] Doing prompt:\\n\\n\")\n\tfmt.Println(string(content))\n\treturn nil\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786916494229},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_nQP2K1UjS9O8pSUKIEsj7895","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Package handler 是 rick 四层架构第二层「调度聚合」。\n//\n// handler 接受 cli 路由与解析后的参数，编排 env → builder → runtime 完成 rick\n// 命令的功能实现，并把 runtime 返回的 sessionID 持久化到 job 目录。它不 import\n// internal/cmd（否则会形成跨包循环依赖）；cli 在调用点把 flag 值解析好，经\n// Options 透传给 handler。\npackage handler\n\n// Options carries flag values resolved by the CLI layer into handler\n// orchestrators. Handlers must not import internal/cmd; the cmd layer passes\n// these explicitly at the call site.\ntype Options struct {\n\tVerbose bool\n\tDryRun  bool\n\tJobID   string\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786916494230},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_02_TQ5auKzlDTRtIpNHJJz04673","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"package cmd\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\n\t\"github.com/spf13/cobra\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/handler\"\n)\n\nfunc NewDoingCmd() *cobra.Command {\n\tvar jobID string\n\tvar easy bool\n\tvar ctxPath string\n\n\tdoingCmd := &cobra.Command{\n\t\tUse:   \"doing [job_id]\",\n\t\tShort: \"Execute tasks in a job\",\n\t\tLong:  `Execute tasks in a job. Supports retry mechanism and automatic commits.`,\n\t\tArgs:  cobra.MaximumNArgs(1),\n\t\tRunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n\t\t\tif GetVerbose() {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Println(\"[INFO] Starting doing phase...\")\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\topts := handler.Options{\n\t\t\t\tVerbose: GetVerbose(),\n\t\t\t\tDryRun:  GetDryRun(),\n\t\t\t\tJobID:   GetJobID(),\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Easy mode: args[0] is requirement (not job_id); --job flag is for resume\n\t\t\tif easy {\n\t\t\t\trequirement := \"\"\n\t\t\t\tif len(args) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\trequirement = args[0]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif GetDryRun() {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn handler.EasyDryRun(requirement, ctxPath)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t// --job flag explicitly set → resume existing session\n\t\t\t\tif jobID == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t\tjobID = GetJobID()\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif jobID != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn handler.ResumeEasy(jobID, opts)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\treturn handler.Easy(requirement, ctxPath, opts)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Normal doing: args[0] is job_id\n\t\t\tif len(args) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\tjobID = args[0]\n\t\t\t} else if jobID == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tjobID = GetJobID()\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif GetDryRun() {\n\t\t\t\treturn handler.DoingDryRun(jobID)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif jobID == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"job ID is required. Usage: rick doing [job_id] or rick doing --job job_id\")\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Validate job ID format\n\t\t\tif err := validateJobID(jobID); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif GetVerbose() {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"[INFO] Executing job: %s\\n\", jobID)\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Execute doing workflow\n\t\t\tif err := handler.Doing(jobID, opts); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Job %s execution completed!\\n\", jobID)\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tdoingCmd.Flags().StringVar(&jobID, \"job\", \"\", \"Job ID to execute\")\n\tdoingCmd.Flags().BoolVar(&easy, \"easy\", false, \"Easy mode: skip plan, start interactive pi session\")\n\tdoingCmd.Flags().StringVar(&ctxPath, \"ctx\", \"\", \"Inherit context from specified .rick directory (easy mode only)\")\n\n\treturn doingCmd\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786916494230},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the current state. The handler `Doing` directly instantiates `runtime.NewPiRuntime`. This violates the DIP principle per KR8.\n\nBut wait — let me think about the scope of task12 again. The task is \"三个 O 端到端验收 + README/wiki 文档同步\". The key results are mostly acceptance checks. But KR8 has a specific check that currently fails.\n\nHowever, I should be careful. Let me re-read the task's \"关键结果\" list. The 关键结果 (Key Results) are the acceptance criteria. KR8 is \"扩展点验收\" with specific greps. Since this is task12 (final acceptance), and the grep fails, I need to determine whether:\n\n1. This is a genuine gap that I need to fix (making handler depend on interface), OR\n2. The grep check is a \"false positive\" because the variable is just named `piRuntime` but actually the intent is that it depends on the interface.\n\nActually, looking at the spec more carefully:\n- §3.5 切换规则: \"新增 dsh 只新增 dshBuilder/dshRuntime/dshEnv 三个实现并注册，cli/handler/方法层 templates 不改。\"\n\nThe handler should NOT construct `runtime.NewPiRuntime` directly. Instead, the composition root (cmd) should construct the runtime and inject it. But the current design has the handler constructing it.\n\nWait, but the spec also says \"例外三（组合根 DIP 越级豁免）：`cmd` 的 `RunE` 懒加载实例化 `piRuntime`/`piEnv`/`pibuilder` 注入 handler，是 DIP 组合根模式，越级豁免。\"\n\nSo the spec explicitly says the composition root (cmd's RunE) should instantiate piRuntime/piEnv/pibuilder and inject into handler. The current code has the handler constructing piRuntime directly, which is NOT the DIP composition root pattern.\n\nSo this is a genuine bug/gap. The handler should receive the runtime via injection (as a parameter or field), and cmd should instantiate it.\n\nHmm, but this is a significant code change for a \"final acceptance\" task. Let me think about whether this is really in scope.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The KR8 says:\n\"扩展点验收：`grep -q 'type Runtime interface' internal/runtime/*.go`、`grep -q 'type RuntimeEnv interface' internal/env/*.go`、`grep -q 'type RuntimeBuilder interface' internal/builder/*.go` 三接口就位；`grep -rniE 'type .*dsh|dshRuntime|dshEnv|dshBuilder|NewDsh' internal/ cmd/` = 0（无 dsh 类型/实现/构造；代码注释中的「dsh」豁免）；`grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` 无命中（handler 依赖接口非具体实现）；`grep -q '\"runtime\"' internal/config/config.go` 字段就位\"\n\nSo the check `grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` 无命中 is a hard acceptance criterion. Currently it's 2 hits. This is a genuine failure.\n\nI think task12 should fix this. The task12 title is \"三个 O 端到端验收 + README/wiki 文档同步\", and KR8 is part of \"三个 O\" acceptance (O2 specifically covers the module responsibilities, and the extension seam is part of the spec).\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the \"三个 O\" acceptance list is:\n- O1 (spec 信息内核)\n- O2 (三层金字塔 + 做薄)\n- O3 (pibuilder pi 对齐)\n\nAnd KR8 \"扩展点验收\" is about the extension seams (Runtime/RuntimeEnv/RuntimeBuilder interfaces + config runtime field + handler not depending on concrete impl). This is related to O2's \"做薄\" and the spec's §3.5.\n\nSo yes, I need to fix the handler to not depend on the concrete `piRuntime`.\n\nBut wait — how big a change is this? Let me think about the minimal fix:\n\nThe handler's `Doing` function constructs `runtime.NewPiRuntime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...)` and calls `piRuntime.Run(...)`.\n\nThe fix: inject the `Runtime` interface into the handler. The composition root (cmd) should construct `runtime.NewPiRuntime` and pass it to `handler.Doing`.\n\nOptions:\n1. Add a `Runtime runtime.Runtime` field to `handler.Options`. Then cmd constructs it and sets it. But `Options` is currently just flag values. Adding a runtime interface to it is a bit odd but workable.\n2. Add a parameter to `Doing(jobID string, opts Options, rt runtime.Runtime)`.\n3. Add a package-level function to set the runtime factory.\n\nGiven the existing pattern (Options struct carries flag values), the cleanest minimal change is to add the runtime to Options, OR add a parameter.\n\nActually, let me check how env and builder are handled in the handler. In `Doing`, it calls:\n- `builder.NewPIBuilder()` directly (concrete pibuilder)\n- `runtime.NewPiRuntime()` directly (concrete piRuntime)\n\nAnd `builder.EnsureTasksJSON`, `builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt`.\n\nWait, the spec says the composition root should instantiate piRuntime/piEnv/pibuilder and inject. But currently the handler also directly constructs `builder.NewPIBuilder()`. Is that also a violation?\n\nKR8 only checks `grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` — it doesn't check for pibuilder in handler. So the pibuilder direct construction is apparently acceptable (or at least not part of the check). Hmm, but that's inconsistent.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. The `pibuilder` is referenced in the spec §3.5 as `RuntimeBuilder`（builder/xxxxbuilder 转义层）. The handler calls `builder.NewPIBuilder()` which is the concrete pibuilder. But KR8's check only covers `piRuntime` in handler. \n\nHmm, this is a bit inconsistent but I should follow the KR exactly. The KR only requires `piRuntime` to not appear in handler. But it also says \"handler 依赖接口非具体实现\" as the rationale.\n\nLet me think about the minimal, correct fix that satisfies the KR and the spec:\n\nThe spec's DIP composition root says cmd instantiates piRuntime/piEnv/pibuilder and injects into handler. But the current code:\n- handler.Doing: constructs `runtime.NewPiRuntime` + `builder.NewPIBuilder`\n- handler's other functions (Easy, Plan, etc.): probably also construct piEnv/pibuilder\n\nLet me check all handler files to understand the full picture before deciding the fix.\n\nActually, let me focus. The task12 is acceptance + docs. The KR8 check specifically says `grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` should be 0. I need to make this pass.\n\nThe minimal fix: rename the local variable from `piRuntime` to something else like `rt` and use the interface type. But that's cosmetic — the check is about whether handler depends on the concrete type `piRuntime` (which would appear as `runtime.NewPiRuntime`). Actually the grep `grep -rn 'piRuntime'` matches BOTH the variable name `piRuntime` AND `runtime.NewPiRuntime`? No wait — `runtime.NewPiRuntime` contains \"PiRuntime\" (capital P), and grep is case-sensitive. `piRuntime` (lowercase p) won't match `NewPiRuntime` (capital P).\n\nLet me check: `grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` matched:\n1. `piRuntime := runtime.NewPiRuntime(cfg.PiPath, cfg.PiExtraArgs...)` — contains `piRuntime` (variable name) and `NewPiRuntime` (capital P).\n2. `_, _, err = piRuntime.Run(method, promptFile, cfg)` — contains `piRuntime`.\n\nSo the matches are the VARIABLE name `piRuntime`, not `NewPiRuntime`. The check `grep -rn 'piRuntime'` (lowercase) catches the variable name.\n\nHmm, so technically, if I rename the variable to `rt`, the grep would no longer match... but `runtime.NewPiRuntime` would still be there. Wait no — `runtime.NewPiRuntime` has capital P, so `grep 'piRuntime'` wouldn't match it.\n\nWait, let me verify. The grep is case-sensitive by default. `NewPiRuntime` = N-e-w-P-i-R-u-n-t-i-m-e. The pattern `piRuntime` = p-i-R-u-n-t-i-m-e. So `NewPiRuntime` contains `PiRuntime` (capital P), not `piRuntime` (lowercase p). So `grep 'piRuntime'` would NOT match `NewPiRuntime`.\n\nSo the actual check only catches the variable name `piRuntime`. If I rename the variable, the grep passes. But that's a superficial fix — the handler would still directly depend on `runtime.NewPiRuntime` (concrete).\n\nHmm. Bu