{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"All 4 matches are in comments (with `//` prefix). These are exempt per KR8 (\"代码注释中的「dsh」豁免\"). But wait — the regex `type .*dsh` would match comments containing \"type ...dsh\"? Let me check. The comment lines are:\n- `// dshEnv 并注册，cli/handler 不改。` — contains \"dshEnv\", matches `dshEnv`\n- `// 唯一实现；将来 dsh 只新增 dshEnv（...）` — contains \"dshEnv\"\n- `// dshBuilder — cli/handler/env 不改；...` — contains \"dshBuilder\"\n- `// means implementing and registering dshRuntime without touching the handlers` — contains \"dshRuntime\"\n\nNone match `type .*dsh` or `NewDsh` — they match the dshRuntime/dshEnv/dshBuilder alternatives. KR8 explicitly says these are \"代码注释中的「dsh」豁免\" (exempt). So 4 comment matches is fine — all are comments, no actual type/impl/constructor.\n\nActually, let me re-read KR8: \"`grep -rniE 'type .*dsh|dshRuntime|dshEnv|dshBuilder|NewDsh' internal/ cmd/` = 0（无 dsh 类型/实现/构造；代码注释中的「dsh」豁免）\"\n\nThis is a bit contradictory: it says the grep should be 0, but comments are exempt. The intent is: no actual dsh types/impl/constructors (only comments). The 4 matches are all comments, so functionally satisfied. But if a strict grep is run, it would return 4 (non-zero). \n\nHmm, this could be an issue if the harness runs the strict grep. But the task12.py test doesn't check this specific grep (it checks the 3 interfaces). Let me check whether the comments should be reworded to avoid the literal tokens dshRuntime/dshEnv/dshBuilder/NewDsh while still conveying the seam.\n\nActually, let me look at the exact KR8 text again:\n\n\"扩展点验收：`grep -q 'type Runtime interface' internal/runtime/*.go`、`grep -q 'type RuntimeEnv interface' internal/env/*.go`、`grep -q 'type RuntimeBuilder interface' internal/builder/*.go` 三接口就位；`grep -rniE 'type .*dsh|dshRuntime|dshEnv|dshBuilder|NewDsh' internal/ cmd/` = 0（无 dsh 类型/实现/构造；代码注释中的「dsh」豁免）；`grep -rn 'piRuntime' internal/handler/` 无命中（handler 依赖接口非具体实现）；`grep -q '\"runtime\"' internal/config/config.go` 字段就位\"\n\nSo the strict acceptance is `= 0`, with comments exempt. The comments in these files mention `dshRuntime`/`dshEnv`/`dshBuilder` literally. If the strict grep includes comments, it returns 4. The \"豁免\" (exemption) note suggests the author knows comments will match and considers them exempt. But to be safe and truly satisfy \"= 0\", I could reword the comments to not use the exact tokens `dshRuntime`/`dshEnv`/`dshBuilder` (e.g., use \"dsh 的 Runtime 实现\" instead of \"dshRuntime\").\n\nActually, let me think about what's the right call here. The task was already marked success with commit a758f6f. The previous attempt's ONLY reported failure was the timestamp. So the dsh grep = 4 (comments) was apparently accepted (or the harness's test didn't check it). The task12.py test doesn't check dsh grep either.\n\nBut to be thorough and avoid any potential strict-check failure, I could reword those 4 comments to avoid the exact tokens. This is low-risk and aligns with the KR8 \"= 0\" intent. Let me do that.\n\nActually wait — let me reconsider. The KR8 says \"代码注释中的「dsh」豁免\" — meaning comments mentioning \"dsh\" are EXEMPT from the =0 requirement. The intent is: no actual dsh type/impl/constructor. The grep pattern is a heuristic; comments are known to trip it and are exempt.\n\nThe 4 matches are all `dshEnv`/`dshBuilder`/`dshRuntime` in comments. Since they're comments, they're exempt. But does the \"= 0\" still apply literally? The parenthetical clarifies the =0 is about \"无 dsh 类型/实现/构造\" (no dsh types/impl/constructors), and comments are exempt.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, and since the task's actual test (task12.py) passes and only checks the 3 interfaces + no piRuntime + config field, I think the comments are fine. But to be safe, I'll reword the comments slightly so the grep `dshRuntime|dshEnv|dshBuilder` returns 0, while `type .*dsh` and `NewDsh` already return 0. This makes the strict grep = 0 c