eRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":31,"totalTokens":27265,"cost":{"input":0.0006699000000000001,"output":0.00010875,"cacheRead":0.0000928,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0008714500000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786917785540,"responseId":"80c82c6c-19c5-4aa2-a52b-d5cdfc8aa0cd","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_fWxLmPIGEsaLWAr2QWEl0950","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 12\ndrwxrwxr-x  2 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 4096 Aug 17 02:51 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 19 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 4096 Aug 17 02:51 ..\n-rwxrwxr-x  1 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 2086 Aug 17 04:44 helper.py\n=== helper.py ===\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Description: rick-gates 门禁 helper — 确定性 doing 门禁校验。\n\n\"\"\"rick-gates 门禁 helper — 确定性 doing 门禁校验。\n\nrick 侧确定性脚本（非 pi extension hook，hook 仅作通知/记录）。runtime.Run 在解析到\nagent_settled（pi 会话结束）后直接调用本脚本校验 doing 门禁，exit 非 0 = 门禁失败。\n\n校验语义（与原 doing_check 三项语义对齐）：\n1. tasks.json 可解析 —— doing/tasks.json 是合法 JSON 且含 tasks 数组。\n2. zombie 检测 —— 无遗留 running 状态任务。\n3. commit_hash 存在 —— status=success 的任务必须有非空 commit_hash。\n\n用法：python3 helper.py <doing_dir>\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n\ndef main(argv):\n    if len(argv) < 2:\n        print(\"usage: helper.py <doing_dir>\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    doing_dir = argv[1]\n    tasks_json_path = os.path.join(doing_dir, \"tasks.json\")\n\n    # 1. tasks.json 可解析\n    try:\n        with open(tasks_json_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - 门禁错误串需兼容任意解析失败\n        print(\"tasks.json 不可解析: %s\" % e, file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    tasks = data.get(\"tasks\")\n    if not isinstance(tasks, list):\n        print(\"tasks.json 缺少 tasks 数组\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\n    for task in tasks:\n        task_id = task.get(\"task_id\", \"?\")\n        status = task.get(\"status\", \"\")\n\n        # 2. zombie 检测\n        if status == \"running\":\n            print(\"zombie running: task %s 仍处于 running 状态\" % task_id, file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n        # 3. commit_hash 存在\n        if status == \"success\":\n            commit_hash = task.get(\"commit_hash\", \"\")\n            if not commit_hash:\n                print(\"missing commit_hash: task %s 状态为 success 但 commit_hash 为空\" % task_id, file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n    print(\"gate passed\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917788414},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me find where tasks.json is written/marked success. The \"mark task success\" was likely done by the agent manually (writing tasks.json). But there might be a helper. Let me look at the mark_task_success_skill and the doing.go, and check how tasks.json is initialized and updated.\n\nActually, the error is a data issue. The task12 agent wrote the timestamp without timezone. I need to fix that.\n\nBut wait - there could be a deeper issue. Let me understand what the \"doing_check\" command does. The prompt says `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. Let me find that command in the codebase.\n\nActually, the prompt says doing 阶段门禁已下沉为 rick-gates 确定性脚本，plan_check/doing_check 已删除. But the \"第二步：格式检查\" still says `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. There's a contradiction. Wait, but the test feedback says \"doing_check failed: ...\". So `doing_check` might still exist, or the error is from the rick-gates helper.\n\nLet me check if `doing_check` still exists in the binary.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_BPYf1lnKXmO5kyPTqV7J8551","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && ./bin/rick tools --help 2>&1 | head -40; echo \"=== doing_check ===\"; ./bin/rick tools doing_check --help 2>&1 | head -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_otnjrIxGRBFbRPUuHAUj3508","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cat .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -100; echo \"=== dir ===\"; ls -la .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":667,"output":435,"cacheRead":27264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":241,"totalTokens":28366,"cost":{"input":0.000290145,"output":0.00037845,"cacheRead":0.000098832,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000767427}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786917788414,"responseId":"1483d628-89a3-4cf9-8b89-5dc31d47e16e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_BPYf1lnKXmO5kyPTqV7J8551","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"rick tools provides a set of validation and management commands for Rick workflows.\n\nThese commands are primarily used by AI agents during the learning phase.\nAn AI agent reads 'rick tools --help' to discover all available tools,\nthen decides which commands to invoke to complete its work.\n\nAvailable subcommands:\n  init-pi         Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + subagent extension\n  learning_check  Validate the learning directory structure for a job (incl. loops/skills format)\n  dream_check     Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/ (incl. loops/skills format)\n\nUsage:\n  rick tools [flags]\n  rick tools [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  dream_check    Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/\n  init-pi        Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + extensions + theme\n  learning_check Validate the learning directory structure for a job\n  theme          List or switch the pi TUI theme\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for tools\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --dry-run      Run in dry-run mode without making changes\n      --job string   Specify job ID (e.g., job_1)\n  -v, --verbose      Enable verbose output\n\nUse \"rick tools [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n=== doing_check ===\nrick tools provides a set of validation and management commands for Rick workflows.\n\nThese commands are primarily used by AI agents during the learning phase.\nAn AI agent reads 'rick tools --help' to discover all available tools,\nthen decides which commands to invoke to complete its work.\n\nAvailable subcommands:\n  init-pi         Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + subagent extension\n  learning_check  Validate the learning directory structure for a job (incl. loops/skills format)\n  dream_check     Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/ (incl. loops/skills format)\n\nUsage:\n  rick tools [flags]\n  rick tools [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  dream_check    Validate dream_run_{job_id}_log.md files in .rick/dream/\n  init-pi        Initialize pi (rick's agent runtime) + extensions + theme\n  learning_check Validate the learning directory structure for a job\n  theme          List or switch the pi TUI theme\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917793904},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_otnjrIxGRBFbRPUuHAUj3508","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# skill:mark-task-success（tasks.json 两阶段提交）\n\n## 触发场景\n\ndoing task 代码已提交（有 commit hash）但 rick-gates 门禁（helper.py）报错：\n- `missing commit_hash`\n- `zombie running`\n\n信号词：`python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py <doing_dir>` 输出上述错误。\n\n## 预期效果\n\n- 一次修复通过 rick-gates 门禁\n- 不需要反复读取 tasks.json 格式或门禁源码\n\n## 核心内容\n\n### 使用辅助脚本（推荐）\n\n```bash\n# 代码已 commit 后，立即执行：\npython3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py --job job_N --task taskX\n# 工具自动读取 HEAD commit hash，更新 tasks.json status=success + commit_hash\n\n# 提交 tasks.json：\ngit add .rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\ngit commit -m \"chore(taskX): mark taskX success in tasks.json\"\n\n# 验证：\npython3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py .rick/jobs/job_N/doing  # 应 exit 0\n```\n\n### 手动修复（备用）\n\n```python\nimport json, subprocess\n\n# 获取 commit hash\nhash_result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\ncommit_hash = hash_result.stdout.strip()\n\n# 更新 tasks.json\nwith open(\".rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\", \"r\") as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nfor task in data[\"tasks\"]:\n    if task[\"task_id\"] == \"taskX\":\n        task[\"status\"] = \"success\"\n        task[\"commit_hash\"] = commit_hash\n        break\n\nwith open(\".rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(data, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n```\n\n### 最优执行序（避免二次失败）\n\n1. 完成代码变更 → `git commit` → 记录 commit hash\n2. `python3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py --job job_N --task taskX`\n3. `git add tasks.json && git commit -m \"chore(taskX): mark success\"`\n4. `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py .rick/jobs/job_N/doing`（此时必过）\n\n### tasks.json 结构说明\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"task1\",\n      \"status\": \"success\",\n      \"commit_hash\": \"40位SHA\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`status=success` + `commit_hash` 非空 → rick-gates 门禁通过。\n=== dir ===\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 4096 Aug  7 19:53 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 19 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 4096 Aug 17 02:51 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 1841 Aug  7 19:53 build_rick.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 2783 Aug  7 19:53 mark_task_success.py\n-rw-r--r--  1 hadoop-recsys hadoop-recsys 2147 Aug 17 04:46 skill.md\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917793904},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `doing_check` no longer exists. The \"第二步：格式检查\" in the prompt still references `bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`, but that command has been deleted (task8). The actual gate is `python3 .rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py .rick/jobs/job_N/doing`.\n\nBut the test feedback says \"doing_check failed: tasks.json not found or invalid: failed to unmarshal tasks.json: parsing time...\". This is likely from a test script that still references the old behavior, OR it's from `learning_check` which reads tasks.json via `LoadTasksJSON`. Wait, actually the error message \"tasks.json not found or invalid: failed to unmarshal tasks.json\" — let me search for this exact string.\n\nActually, let me check the learning.go which does LoadTasksJSON and the error format.\n\nActually, looking at learning.go line 124: `return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"failed to load tasks.json: %w\", err)`. Not exactly matching.\n\nThe error in feedback: \"tasks.json not found or invalid: failed to unmarshal tasks.json: parsing time ...\". Let me search for \"tasks.json not found or invalid\".","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_UdSrojOr2Dc8ikuM9v3d0800","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"tasks.json not found or invalid\\|not found or invalid\" --include=\"*.go\" internal/ cmd/ pkg/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== broader ===\"; grep -rn \"not found or invalid\" . --include=\"*.go\" 2>/dev/null"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_0z7Objz30OeNO4sHVrPi8268","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cat .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1393,"output":437,"cacheRead":28288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":251,"totalTokens":30118,"cost":{"input":0.000605955,"output":0.00038019000000000003,"cacheRead":0.000102544,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001088689}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786917793905,"responseId":"a77513a4-d87f-4bee-a005-af41344a66f9","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_UdSrojOr2Dc8ikuM9v3d0800","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== broader ===\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1786917799444},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_0z7Objz30OeNO4sHVrPi8268","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Description: Mark a task as success in tasks.json with the current HEAD commit hash, then commit and verify doing_check passes.\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\n\n\ndef get_commit_hash():\n    r = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if r.returncode != 0:\n        return None, r.stderr.strip()\n    return r.stdout.strip(), None\n\n\ndef find_rick_root():\n    path = os.getcwd()\n    while path != \"/\":\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(path, \".rick\")):\n            return path\n        path = os.path.dirname(path)\n    return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Mark a task as success in tasks.json\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--job\", required=True, help=\"Job ID, e.g. job_17\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--task\", required=True, help=\"Task ID, e.g. task1\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--commit\", help=\"Commit hash (defaults to git HEAD)\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--test\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Self-test mode\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if args.test:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": True, \"errors\": [], \"note\": \"self-test ok\"}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        return\n\n    root = find_rick_root()\n    if not root:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [\"cannot find .rick root\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    tasks_json = os.path.join(root, \".rick\", \"jobs\", args.job, \"doing\", \"tasks.json\")\n    if not os.path.exists(tasks_json):\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"tasks.json not found: {tasks_json}\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    commit_hash = args.commit\n    if not commit_hash:\n        commit_hash, err = get_commit_hash()\n        if err:\n            print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"git rev-parse failed: {err}\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n    with open(tasks_json, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        data = json.load(f)\n\n    now = datetime.now(tz=timezone(timedelta(hours=8))).isoformat()\n    found = False\n    for task in data[\"tasks\"]:\n        if task[\"task_id\"] == args.task:\n            task[\"status\"] = \"success\"\n            task[\"commit_hash\"] = commit_hash\n            task[\"updated_at\"] = now\n            found = True\n            break\n\n    if not found:\n        print(json.dumps({\"pass\": False, \"errors\": [f\"task {args.task} not found in tasks.json\"]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    data[\"updated_at\"] = now\n    with open(tasks_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n    print(json.dumps({\"pass\": True, \"errors\": [], \"task\": args.task, \"commit_hash\": commit_hash}, ensure_ascii=False))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786917799444},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mark_task_success.py uses `datetime.now(tz=timezone(timedelta(hours=8))).isoformat()` which produces a timezone-aware timestamp like `2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297+08:00`. But the tasks.json shows `\"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297\"` without timezone. That's weird.\n\nWait, let me re-read the tasks.json. The task12 updated_at is `\"2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297\"` — no timezone. But the mark_task_success.py uses `.isoformat()` with tz. Hmm, but maybe the agent manually edited tasks.json (not using mark_task_success.py), and wrote `datetime.now()` without tz.\n\nActually wait, the task12 agent probably manually edited tasks.json. The previous commits show `1608b3f chore(task12): mark task12 success in tasks.json`. The updated_at got written without timezone.\n\nRegardless, the fix is to correct the tasks.json timestamp. Let me check the actual file bytes for the exact string.\n\nActually I already saw it: task12's `updated_at` = `\"2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297\"` and its top-level `updated_at` = `\"2026-08-17T05:31:25.583021028+08:00\"` (wait, let me re-read).\n\nFrom the read earlier:\n```\n\"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T05:31:25.583021028+08:00\",  <- top-level\n...\ntask11 updated_at: \"2026-08-17T05:31:25.582031614+08:00\"\ntask12: \"created_at\": \"2026-08-17T00:59:46.783995764+08:00\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297\", \"commit_hash\": \"a758f6fae396ea85b019dd2d0eff29e7839a559b\"\n```\n\nSo task12's updated_at lacks timezone AND lacks the fractional seconds fully (it has 6 digits: `.789297`, which is microseconds). The mark_task_success.py would produce something like `2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297+08:00` with timezone. So the agent manually wrote it.\n\nAlso notice the top-level `updated_at` is still `2026-08-17T05:31:25.583021028+08:00` (from task11), not updated to task12's time. But that's a minor inconsistency, not a parse error.\n\nSo the fix: fix task12's updated_at to include `+08:00` timezone (matching the format used elsewhere). \n\nBut wait — I need to think more broadly. The task is task12: \"三个 O 端到端验收 + README/wiki 文档同步\". The task has already been done (there are commits). But the doing_check gate failed because of the malformed timestamp. \n\nActually, let me re-read the \"Test Execution Feedback\" at the end of the prompt:\n\n```\n=== Attempt 1 ===\ndoing_check failed: tasks.json not found or invalid: failed to unmarshal tasks.json: parsing time \"2026-08-17T06:01:04.789297\" as \"2006-01-02T15:04:05Z07:00\": cannot parse \"\" as \"Z07:00\"\n```\n\nThis is the failure that caused this retry. So my job is to fix this and complete the task.\n\nThe error message \"tasks.json not found or invalid: failed to unmarshal tasks.json\" — I couldn't find this exact string in the Go code. Let me search more broadly, maybe in a test script or in the rick-gates extension.\n\nActually, maybe it's from `learning_check` or from