njection**：需要在 `rick plan` 或 `rick easy` 会话中嵌入新的结构化行为时\n- **test-script-practices**：在 plan 或 doing 阶段编写/调试任务测试脚本（`.rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tests/taskN.py`）时使用，特别是\n- **verify-go-changes**：修改了 Go 源文件后，需要验证编译通过、单元测试和集成测试通过时使用。\n- **zero-retry-task-design**：plan 阶段分解需求为多个 task.md 时使用，目标是让每个 task 在 doing 阶段一次性完成，无需重试。\n\n\n---\n\n## Job 上下文\n\n/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_N/doing/debug\n\n---\n\n\nexit=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786918028044},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `human-loop test-topic --dry-run` and `easy -r test --dry-run` work correctly (exit 0, contain pi trigger syntax). My earlier test just lacked required args.\n\nNow let me check the remaining: `learning --dry-run`, `dream --dry-run`, `ctrl --dry-run --job job_N`.\n\n- `learning --dry-run`: exit 0 but my grep didn't find \"pi trigger syntax\". Let me check its output more carefully. The learning dry-run uses `buildLearningPrompt` which may not contain workflowScript. The KR5 requirement is \"含 pi 触发语法\". What counts as \"pi 触发语法\"? Likely `--append-system-prompt`, or `runtime.CallCLI`, or explicit pi invocation. Let me look at the learning prompt output.\n\n- `dream --dry-run`: FOUND `{{` placeholder. This is a real issue — the dream template still has `{{` placeholders that aren't filled.\n\n- `ctrl --dry-run --job job_N`: exit 1. Need to check why.\n\nLet me examine these three.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_eCuMIaHvP3yL3vOhpsQ88015","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"===== learning --dry-run =====\"; ./bin/rick learning --dry-run 2>&1 | head -80; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_VilX6kTsNUID2x7OcaMY8026","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"===== ctrl --dry-run --job job_N =====\"; ./bin/rick ctrl --dry-run --job job_N 2>&1 | head -60; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"