un output must contain loops reference; output snippet:\\n%s\", truncate(output, 500))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc truncate(s string, n int) string {\n\tif len(s) <= n {\n\t\treturn s\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s...(truncated)\", s[:n])\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786918083885},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dryrun integration test is basic. It doesn't check pi trigger syntax in learning.\n\nOK, let me step back and take stock of the actual state and what's needed:\n\nThe task12 is essentially complete (commits done). The reported failure was the tasks.json timestamp, which I've fixed. Additional cleanup: I rewrote 4 comments to make the dsh grep = 0.\n\nThe KR5 \"含 pi 触发语法且无 {{\" is a key result. Let me verify the actual state of each dry-run command against this more carefully, and understand what \"pi 触发语法\" means. Given the O3 context (pibuilder pi 对齐), the key transformation is:\n- plan/doing/easy/human-loop/ctrl/dream prompts now use `subagent({ workflowScript: ... })` + `runs.run` + `agent:'xxx'` instead of natural language \"SPAWN Sub Agent\".\n- learning is a single pi session (no subagents), so it may not have \"pi 触发语法\" in the prompt — but it's still \"pi 对齐\" because it's driven by `runtime.CallCLI`.\n\nActually, let me re-read the task's O3 acceptance (from 任务目标):\n\n\"O3（pibuilder pi 对齐）：模板中 `workflowScript`/`runs.run` 出现 >0；think/research/exporter 落盘为 pi agent；门禁由 rick-gates hook + 脚本承载；自然语言触发词下降\"\n\nSo O3 is about the templates containing workflowScript/runs.run > 0 (which the task12.py test checks via files_with_match(WORKFLOW_RE) >= 1). It's not about EVERY command's dry-run containing them.\n\nKR5's \"含 pi 触发语法\" is a separate acceptance. Let me interpret \"pi 触发语法\" more loosely: it could be `workflowScript`, `runs.run`, `subagent(`, `agent:'`, `--append-system-prompt`, or the pi CLI invocation. For learning, the prompt references `rick tools learning_check` and the execution is via pi CLI. Hmm.\n\nActually, w